    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG McKenna Healy are delighted to present The Pink House, a charming double-fronted, three-bedroom period residence occupying a generous site on the highly convenient Channel Road.\n\nWhile the property requires complete refurbishment and modernisation, it retains an abundance of original charm and character, including attractive period fireplaces. Its distinctive double-fronted façade and well-proportioned accommodation provide an excellent opportunity for the discerning purchaser to restore and transform this unique home to their own taste.\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hallway with a reception room positioned on either side, while a kitchen/dining room is located to the rear. A utility room and shower room complete the ground-floor accommodation. Upstairs, there are three bedrooms and a family bathroom.\n\nThe property stands on an excellent site with gardens to the front and rear, together with a large side entrance offering valuable access and further potential, subject to the necessary planning permission. The private south-facing rear garden is ideally positioned to enjoy sunlight throughout the day, while the front provides convenient off-street parking.\n\nThe location is a particular highlight, with Rush town centre and its wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities all within easy walking distance. The local national school is just a stone's throw away, as is the beautiful sandy South Beach.\n\nRush is a thriving seaside town offering an excellent quality of life within easy commuting distance of Dublin City Centre. Both bus and rail services are readily available, while the M1, M50 and Dublin Airport can all be reached within approximately 20 minutes. The town is also home to a superb range of sporting and recreational facilities, including golf, sailing, cricket, GAA and soccer, together with a choice of primary and secondary schools.\n\nThe Pink House represents a rare opportunity to restore a character-filled period home on a superb south-facing site in the heart of Rush."
      },
      {
